{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Blessed be HaShem, the Elohim of Shem.</b> Blessed be HaShem, who is the master and elohim of Shem — for he has no master but HaShem, Elohim. Corresponding to the fact that he cursed this one with servitude, he blessed that one with freedom." "<b>And Canaan was a servant to them.</b> To Shem and to his Elohim — a hewer of wood and a drawer of water for the altar and for the courtyard." "<b>And Canaan was a servant to them.</b> To the seed of Shem the land was given as a heritage, as it is written: ויהי כנען עבד למו."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {2 "The lemma is repeated as a heading for a second interpretation; the brackets in the source suggest it may be marked as secondary or additional in the witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:42.824764315Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}